<title>Connect your agent — Valio Aimo</title>
<style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;line-height:1.6}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:24px 0}td,th{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}pre{background:#f4f4f4;padding:18px;overflow:auto}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}a{color:#175d45}</style></head><body>
<h1>Connect your procurement agent</h1>
<p>Start with an operator-issued sandbox credential. The operator provisions the scenario and provides its base URL, customer scope and any buyer mandate. Use an isolated sandbox deployment with its own database, signing keys, credentials and policy; set GATEWAY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox. Do not point scenario clients at live demo storage. Orders are fixed-price, <strong>gateway-simulated</strong>; no order is sent to Valio Aimo.</p>
<nav><a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI</a> · <a href="/mcp/server-card">MCP server card (draft)</a> · <a href="/.well-known/agent-card.json">A2A card</a> · <a href="/developers/tools.json">Tool schemas</a> · <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> · <a href="/.well-known/jwks.json">JWKS</a> · <a href="/v1/meta">Pinned versions</a></nav>
<h2>Endpoints and authentication</h2>
<p>REST base: <code>{{BASE_URL}}/v1</code>. MCP Streamable HTTP: <code>{{BASE_URL}}/mcp</code> (POST JSON-RPC; GET is the protocol stream, not a card). A2A 1.0 JSON-RPC: <code>{{BASE_URL}}/a2a</code> with <code>A2A-Version: 1.0</code>. Public discovery begins at <a href="/.well-known/ai-catalog.json">AI catalog</a>. Use TLS in production and configure GATEWAY_PUBLIC_URL to the public origin so MCP accepts its Host and Origin. Runtime tools/list and initialize are authoritative; the draft server card is advisory.</p>
<p>Private agent HTTP calls, including MCP initialize, need <code>Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN</code>. Human REST calls can instead use a session cookie from POST /v1/auth/login with X-CSRF-Token on mutations. X-Agent-Id grants no authority. An optional buyer-issued VC-JWT goes in <code>Agent-Mandate</code> on each request. GET /v1/me and MCP get_agent_context show only your principal, customers, standing constraints, effective limits, rolling budget and supported operations. Operator and buyer approver credentials are separate from agent credentials.</p>
<h2>MCP client configurations</h2>
<p>The console operator issues keys with POST /v1/connections and an Idempotency-Key, supplying agent_id, client and known customer_ids. Copy the vtg_live_ (or sandbox vtg_sbx_) key from the initial 201 response; exact replays return key: null. Tenant admins use /v1/tenant/connections with their own account. GET /v1/connections lists key prefixes and last use; DELETE /v1/connections/{connection_id} revokes the key for both REST and MCP. New agents require human approval; an existing agent keeps its mandate and autonomy. The client field records a tool preference and grants no extra authority. ChatGPT and other remote clients can use OAuth code/PKCE sign-in through /oauth/authorize. The existing operator-consented buyer /mcp flow is also supported on the same endpoints; it keeps its own consent requests and grants.</p>
<p>Claude Code, from any directory, using the issued remote credential:</p>
<pre data-config="claude-code">claude mcp add --transport http valio-aimo "${GATEWAY_URL}/mcp" --header "Authorization: Bearer ${AGENT_TOKEN}"</pre>
<p>Claude Desktop local stdio configuration (replace absolute paths and the operator-provisioned agent ID). Stdio is a trusted local process: it loads server credentials and policy from its environment; it does not use remote Bearer authentication. Run it on the gateway host only. Never copy operator or supplier secrets onto an outside buyer's device. Optional buyer VC: append --mandate /absolute/path/mandate.jwt.</p>
<pre data-config="claude-desktop">{"mcpServers":{"valio-aimo":{"command":"/absolute/repo/backend/.venv/bin/python","args":["-m","app.mcp_server","--agent-id","issued-agent"],"cwd":"/absolute/repo/backend"}}}</pre>
<p>Generic MCP CLI (install <code>mcp[cli]==2.3.0</code> to include the optional Typer CLI dependency) (development inspector, gateway host):</p>
<pre data-config="mcp-cli">cd /absolute/repo/backend
MCP_AGENT_ID=issued-agent .venv/bin/mcp dev app/mcp_entry.py</pre>
<p>Raw stdio command: <code>cd /absolute/repo/backend &amp;&amp; .venv/bin/python -m app.mcp_server --agent-id issued-agent</code>. Standalone Streamable HTTP on port 8001 is also available by adding --http --port 8001; the main API serves the discoverable multi-agent /mcp on its own port. Run one process per database: stop the gateway before using a standalone entry point on its database, or set DB_PATH to a separate isolated database.</p>
<h2>Deterministic Python reference buyer</h2>
<p>From the repository root, install pinned clients/python/requirements.txt in a separate venv, then export GATEWAY_URL and AGENT_TOKEN using clients/python/.env.example. Optional AGENT_MANDATE is the VC-JWT itself. Run <code>python clients/python/reference_buyer.py --scenario full_stock</code> or <code>--scenario split_stock</code>. No LLM is used. The client initializes MCP, lists tools, reads context, selects a stored plan, quotes, orders, follows next_action and verifies the Ed25519 receipt against public JWKS. full_stock requests 10 L; split_stock requests 400 L and requires a provisioned split plan plus a policy requiring human approval. The client sleeps on WAIT_FOR_APPROVAL and polls status; it cannot approve its own order. The operator approves in the console or authenticated REST inbox. Other scenario fixtures an operator may provision: missing_evidence, shifted_date, expired_quote, approval_time_stock_change and supplier_timeout. This kit does not provision or reset sandbox state.</p>
<h2 id="rules">Procurement rules</h2>
<p>A need requires customer_id, intent, quantity {value, unit} and deliver_by. Units are L, KG or SALES_UNIT. Values are strict positive numbers up to 1,000,000. deliver_by is today through +60 days in Europe/Helsinki. Explicit quote quantities are whole sales units, including KG, in allowed_lot_size steps with a minimum step of one, and at least minimum_order_quantity. Minimum quantity and order multiple are independent. Do not treat a sales unit as one litre. Tool and field tables below carry the complete schemas.</p>
<p>Customer standing constraints are unioned with each request at lookup, quote, order and approval. Missing allergen evidence never proves absence. Hard constraints cannot be approved away. Preferences may produce substitutes requiring approval. Use a returned plan_ref, or explicit lines with need_ref from the stored lookup. Prices cannot be negotiated. Quotes expire at the earliest applicable price validity, future cut-off or 30 minutes. On REFRESH_QUOTE, create a new quote and inspect its fixed total.</p>
<p>Orders become CONFIRMED, PENDING_APPROVAL, PENDING_EXECUTION or REJECTED. PENDING_EXECUTION carries RETRY_SAME_COMMAND and a positive retry_after_seconds; repeat the original placement key to reconcile its durable supplier intent. Authority is rechecked before any new supplier submission. Pending orders return next_action=WAIT_FOR_APPROVAL and poll_after_seconds. A human reviews the evidence_revision. Changed evidence produces REVIEW_UPDATED_EVIDENCE and must be reviewed again; pending orders may expire. Follow next_action, never infer recovery from error prose. RETRY_SAME_COMMAND means wait retry_after_seconds and resend identical arguments and idempotency key, including after a lost response. LOOKUP_REQUIRED means refresh lookup; FIX_REQUEST means correct schema fields; CONTACT_ADMIN means replace credentials or obtain scope; STOP means halt. REST failures use RFC 9457 application/problem+json, MCP uses isError and identical structured content. X-Correlation-Id links requests.</p>
<p>Lookup, mutation and read token buckets are shared across REST, MCP and A2A per principal. Default capacities/refill per minute are 60/60, 120/120 and 600/600; operator policy may tighten them. Read get_agent_context for effective buckets. RATE_LIMITED (429) and upstream 502/503 retry guidance carry intervals. Supplier calls are paced at 5/s; 429 pauses uncached calls for Retry-After (default 30 seconds). Cached results can continue.</p>
<h2>REST walkthrough</h2>
<p>Execute in bash with GATEWAY_URL and AGENT_TOKEN exported, jq installed and DELIVER_BY set to a date within 60 days. The response files are temporary. This example needs the full_stock fixture. Agent credentials cannot approve; an approver uses POST /v1/approvals/{id}/approve with approver and the current evidence_revision.</p>
<pre data-walkthrough="rest">set -eu
CONNECT_DIR=$(mktemp -d)
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/v1/me" -H "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/me.json"
CUSTOMER_ID=$(jq -r '.customer_ids[0]' "$CONNECT_DIR/me.json")
jq -n --arg customer "$CUSTOMER_ID" --arg day "$DELIVER_BY" '{customer_id:$customer,intent:"lactose-free milk",search_terms:["milk"],required_claims:["FREE_FROM_LACTOSE"],exclude_allergens:["AE"],quantity:{value:10,unit:"L"},deliver_by:$day}' &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/need.json"
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/v1/offers" -H "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-binary @"$CONNECT_DIR/need.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/offers.json"
jq --arg customer "$CUSTOMER_ID" --arg day "$DELIVER_BY" '{customer_id:$customer,deliver_by:$day,plan_ref:{lookup_id:.lookup_id,plan_index:0}}' "$CONNECT_DIR/offers.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/quote-request.json"
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/v1/quotes" -H "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H "Idempotency-Key: connect-quote-$(basename "$CONNECT_DIR")" --data-binary @"$CONNECT_DIR/quote-request.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/quote.json"
jq '{quote_id:.id}' "$CONNECT_DIR/quote.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/order-request.json"
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/v1/orders" -H "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H "Idempotency-Key: connect-order-$(basename "$CONNECT_DIR")" --data-binary @"$CONNECT_DIR/order-request.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/order.json"
ORDER_ID=$(jq -r '.id' "$CONNECT_DIR/order.json")
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/v1/orders/$ORDER_ID" -H "Authorization: Bearer $AGENT_TOKEN" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/order.json"
curl --fail-with-body -sS "$GATEWAY_URL/.well-known/jwks.json" &gt; "$CONNECT_DIR/jwks.json"
python clients/python/verify_receipt.py "$CONNECT_DIR/order.json" --jwks "$CONNECT_DIR/jwks.json" --customer "$CUSTOMER_ID" --agent "$(jq -r '.principal.id' "$CONNECT_DIR/me.json")"</pre>
<h2>Verify evidence</h2>
<p>Keep the order JSON and JWKS. The independent verifier above checks detached Ed25519 JWS, customer, agent and gateway-simulated commitment. Tampered totals or status fail verification. A verified receipt proves this gateway's recorded decision, not supplier fulfilment. Signed quotes can also be verified offline with backend/scripts/verify_quote.py; retain quote.signature and its SHA-256 digest in the receipt. The authenticated order timeline and UBL export are at /v1/orders/{id}/timeline and /v1/orders/{id}/ubl.</p>
<h2 id="failures">Connection failures</h2>
<table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Next step</th></tr>
<tr><td>401, CONTACT_ADMIN; expired, revoked or unknown credential</td><td>Ask the issuer for a replacement sandbox credential, update Authorization, reconnect and read context. Do not retry a rejected key indefinitely. Static operator-issued keys remain valid until removed or rotated.</td></tr>
<tr><td>404, 405, HTML or JSON parsing error</td><td>Check the base URL and transport. REST is /v1; MCP is /mcp; /mcp/server-card is metadata. Use POST for MCP JSON-RPC, never stdio frames over HTTP.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Unsupported protocol version / initialize failure / 400</td><td>Read supportedProtocolVersions from the draft card and pinned /v1/meta; use the pinned mcp==2.3.0 client and initialize before tools/list. A2A requires version 1.0.</td></tr>
<tr><td>403, CONTACT_ADMIN, missing customer scope or mandate</td><td>Compare get_agent_context with the requested customer, then ask the buyer/operator for the correct scope or VC. Changing X-Agent-Id cannot grant it.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Lost connection / stale MCP session / 404 session</td><td>Reconnect and initialize again, list tools and read context. Retry an ambiguous mutation with the same key and payload; never create a new order key because a response was lost. This HTTP endpoint is stateless; it requires no session-ID persistence.</td></tr></table>
<h2>Accounts and connections</h2>
<p>Human accounts sign in with email and password at POST /v1/auth/login. HttpOnly session cookies require X-CSRF-Token on mutations. Tenant admins manage their team, agents, signed mandates and connections under /v1/tenant. Approvers sign off their tenant orders; viewers read evidence. Platform admins use /v1/operator across tenants. Human decisions return a summary and a single-use five-minute confirmation token before applying the confirmed retry.</p>
<p>GET /v1/connect/catalog?audience=buyer|tenant|operator lists MCP, REST, A2A, webhook and tool-pack types, clients and current availability. API-key connections issue vtg_live_ or vtg_sbx_ keys once. Instructions, rotate (up to 24 h overlap) and revoke live under /v1/tenant/connections/{id}. GET /v1/me shows the connection, tenant and allowed customers. Bearer keys and legacy OPERATOR_TOKEN remain supported. OAuth code/PKCE is available for remote MCP and A2A, with signed-in human consent at /oauth/authorize. Human MCP resources are /mcp/tenant and /mcp/operator; A2A resources are /a2a/tenant and /a2a/operator. Tenant/operator webhooks and tool packs use the same audience. MCP decisions require input_required confirmation; A2A and REST use a single-use five-minute confirmation_token. GET /v1/connect/tool-pack?format=openai|anthropic|gemini&amp;audience=buyer|tenant|operator generates function declarations and a REST executor. Read the availability flags before offering a client flow.</p>
<h2>Generated tool and field reference</h2>
<p>Generated by backend/scripts/build_developer_docs.py from the same registered schemas as runtime tools/list. The divergence acceptance test checks this page and the complete JSON schemas.</p>
